describer", "content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was happening at a particular time in the past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense.</br> The Past Continuous talks about a longer \u2018background' action.</br> The Simple Past talks about talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the words <span class=\"strong\">when</span> and <span class=\"strong\">while</span> before the longer action."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Susan called me while I was making dinner."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Dave wrote his essay while watching TV."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "nonetheless"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in spite of what has just been said"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Don't get me wrong, I always like to see the Red Sox win but it was a great hit by Toronto, nonetheless."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about sports."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inning"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "one of the nine parts of a game in which each team bats"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You weren't looking too well after the ninth inning."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob04aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "traitor"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a person who is not loyal to his or her own country, friends, or team"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You'll sound like a traitor."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob04aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "league"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of sports teams that play against each other"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I was thinking about joining the local baseball league."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob04aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "meringue"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a light, sweet mixture of egg whites and sugar that is baked and used as a topping for pies and cakes"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Alright then...pass me some of that lemon meringue pie!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob04aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "coming down with"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "feeling the start of a sickness"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Maybe you're coming down with something."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob04aud06"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le15ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Silent UE"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Some sounds in the English language are silent. For example, when <span class=\"strong\">\"ue\"</span> is after a <span class=\"strong\">\"g\"</span> or a <span class=\"strong\">\"q\"</span> at the end of a word, it is usually silent."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When a word ends with <span class=\"strong\">-gue</span>, it makes a <span class=\"strong\">\"g\"</span> sound.<br><span class=\"italic\">For example: <ul><li>dialo<span class=\"underline\">gue</span></li><li>lea<span class=\"underline\">gue</span></li><li>fati<span class=\"underline\">gue</span></li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When a word ends with <span class=\"strong\">-que</span>, it makes a <span class=\"strong\">\"k\"</span> sound.<br> <span class=\"italic\">For example:<br><ul><li>anti<span class=\"underline\">que</span></li><li>bis<span class=\"underline\">que</span></li><li>uni<span class=\"underline\">que</span></li></ul></span> "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sometimes a <span class=\"strong\">\"ue\"</span> sound is silent in the middle of a word.<br><span class=\"italic\">For example:<br><ul><li>vag<span class=\"underline\">ue</span>ly</li><li>uniq<span class=\"underline\">ue</span>ness</li><li>antiq<span class=\"underline\">ue</span>ness</li></ul></span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'm feeling a little fatigued."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I was thinking about joining the local baseball league."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research baseball in your city or country. Is it or was it a popular sport? Write 1 sentence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Is there a league? How many teams play in the league? Write 2 sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "What types of injuries or health problems do you think baseball players get? Write 2 sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present the information to a partner."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I complete research on a sport. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write 2 sentences about baseball leagues."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about the health problems of baseball players."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I present the information to a partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}